\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Gaussian scan visualization of the Mahalanobis scoring step. (a)~Sequential baseline: covariance inversions are computed one spatial position at a time, leaving all parallel compute resources idle between iterations. (b)~Vectorized optimized pipeline: the pre-computed inverse covariance tensor $\mathbf  {C}^{-1}$ enables all 3{,}136 positions to be scored simultaneously via batched tensor contractions, saturating SIMD and GPU thread resources. An animated rendering of the full scan progression is provided as supplementary material (\texttt  {gaussian\_scan.gif}).}}{3}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gaussian_scan}{{1}{3}{Gaussian scan visualization of the Mahalanobis scoring step. (a)~Sequential baseline: covariance inversions are computed one spatial position at a time, leaving all parallel compute resources idle between iterations. (b)~Vectorized optimized pipeline: the pre-computed inverse covariance tensor $\mathbf {C}^{-1}$ enables all 3{,}136 positions to be scored simultaneously via batched tensor contractions, saturating SIMD and GPU thread resources. An animated rendering of the full scan progression is provided as supplementary material (\texttt {gaussian\_scan.gif})}{figure.caption.2}{}}
